WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.960
Many of the stars of Superbad were launched
to instant fame after the movie became a giant

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.260
hit, but not all of them were so lucky.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.240
Whatever happened to Martha MacIsaac?

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.940
Here's what she's been up to and how she looks
today.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:17.960
In 2011, MacIsaac took on the lead role in
Hoax for the Holidays, a little-known Canadian

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.380
Christmas movie with an unusual premise.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:25.230
She plays a rebellious teen who hoodwinks
the residents of her small town when she throws

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:29.660
her coffee against the wall of a donut store
and manipulates the stain so that it resembles

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.140
the face of Jesus Christ.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:32.420
"What is it?"

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:35.940
"Jesus Christ."

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.460
For the Canadian MacIsaac, the film was very
much a homecoming, as she had worked with

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:45.080
a lot of the same crew members on the CBC
TV series Emily of New Moon when she was a

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:45.580
kid.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.240
In an interview with AXS, she said,

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.640
"They were all like long-lost family.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.560
To get to come back and see all of them as
an adult was incredible."

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:59.559
In 2012, MacIsaac went from playing a troublesome
teen in small-town Canada to playing a troublesome

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:00.860
teen in the White House.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:06.960
She was a main cast member in all thirteen
episodes of the NBC sitcom 1600 Penn as the

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:10.540
ordinarily straitlaced but accidentally pregnant
First Daughter.

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:15.340
Bill Pullman, perhaps best-known for playing
the president in the sci-fi classic Independence

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:20.580
Day, once again took on the role of Commander
in Chief, much to the amusement of his co-stars.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:25.180
In an interview with She Said Media Said,
MacIsaac confirmed that Pullman could handle

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:26.480
the teasing, saying,

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.360
"He's one of the nicest and down-to-earth
men I've ever had the pleasure of meeting.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.120
He's just one of those rare gems."

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:37.560
MacIsaac's character also bore some coincidental
familiarity, as she was named Becca, just

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.000
like her Superbad character.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:44.420
Sadly for the actress, her first full-time
American TV show didn't last very long.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:48.880
It suffered mediocre reviews and was axed
by NBC after a single season.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:55.420
MacIsaac married producer and director Torre
Catalano in 2010, but sadly, their union ended

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.620
just five years later.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:02.000
In that time they worked together on a handful
of projects, the first of which was a 2013

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.620
short named Seasick Sailor.

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:09.640
The two split in 2015, the same year that
Catalano's debut feature film, Almost Anything,

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:11.760
later renamed Milwaukee, was released.

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:16.720
It's a saucy dramedy about a bunch of 30-somethings
testing the limits of monogamy.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:20.940
It features MacIsaac as Greta, a woman struggling
with trust issues.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:25.260
That premise seems a little awkward now that
we know her marriage to Catalano was on the

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.180
rocks at the time.

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.220
Post-divorce, MacIsaac has found a new man
in her life.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:33.680
His name is Kyle McCullough, and he's dabbled
in acting, but he now appears to be focused

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.640
on working in the video game industry.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:40.990
In December 2018, the two had a surprise wedding,
with none other than Paul McCartney helping

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:42.480
McCullough out with the proposal.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:48.120
MacIsaac isn't particularly close to any of
the guys from Superbad, but she and Emma Stone

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:51.960
remain near and dear friends, having even
spent a few years living together.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:57.880
In 2012, MacIsaac presented her pal with the
first ever MTV Trailblazer Award, a title

00:02:57.880 --> 00:03:00.580
that Stone has more than lived up to in the
years since.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:05.530
She got her first Oscar nomination for 2014's
Birdman and then won a couple of years later

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:06.540
for La La Land.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:10.940
And just like best friends should be, MacIsaac
has been right by Stone's side every step

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:11.660
of the way.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:17.260
"Emma has proven herself as one of the most
enduring and captivating actresses of our

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:17.900
generation.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.500
She's a gifted entertainer and a very dear
friend."

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:27.440
In 2017, MacIsaac joined fellow actresses
Ahna O'Reilly and Sugar Lyn Beard for a pre-Oscars

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.040
get together, with all three sporting t-shirts
in support of Stone's bid for Best Actress.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:36.580
A couple of months after the Oscar buzz had
died down, Stone and MacIsaac went to a relaxing

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:42.060
trip to Sonoma in northern California, a picturesque
city located in the heart of a world-renowned

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.200
winemaking region.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:49.840
MacIsaac's most recent major film role was
in 2017's sports biopic Battle of the Sexes.

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:56.200
It's based on the true story of the 1973 exhibition
match between Billie Jean King and Bobby Riggs,

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.260
a historic moment in the history of women's
tennis.

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:04.660
King won in three straight sets, meaning Riggs,
who had belittled women's tennis in the media,

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:05.760
had to eat his words.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:10.000
King was played by Emma Stone, and her bestie
was right there alongside her.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:15.020
MacIsaac had the honor of playing Jane "Peaches"
Bartkowicz, who was a member of the Original

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:19.360
9, a group of female players that included
King and changed tennis forever.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.300
As it turns out, the fact that MacIsaac and
Stone are BFFs in real life actually helped

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.240
her land the role.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:28.010
Co-director Valerie Faris told CinemaBlend,

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:32.160
"She and Emma are friends, and it just felt
like if we build this group of women that

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.380
have a certain camaraderie, that can't hurt."

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:39.120
In addition to Battle of the Sexes, MacIsaac
has appeared in a couple of small, independent

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:40.600
films the past few years.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:44.600
First up was Unicorn Store, the directorial
debut of Brie Larson.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.260
It features Larson as a woman who receives
a mysterious invitation to fulfill her dreams.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:54.520
The film also stars Samuel L. Jackson, Joan
Cusack, and Bradley Whitford, and it had its

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:58.340
world premiere at the 2017 Toronto International
Film Festival.

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:04.320
Next up was the thriller What Keeps You Alive,
which premiered at the 2018 South by Southwest

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:04.820
Festival.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:08.620
It's about a couple celebrating their first
anniversary at a remote cabin.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:13.560
MacIsaac plays a former childhood friend who
arouses suspicion when she shows up.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:18.620
As for the future, MacIsaac unfortunately
doesn't appear to have any film or TV projects

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:20.060
arriving anytime soon.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:24.980
But judging by her Instagram, she's been keeping
herself busy by baking delicious-looking cakes.

